.TH RESIZE.EXFAT 8 "October 2026" "exfatprogs" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
resize.exfat \- experimental offline resize of an exFAT volume image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B resize.exfat
.I image
.B --size
.I size
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RB [ --journal
.IR directory ]
.br
.B resize.exfat
.I image
.B --info
.br
.B resize.exfat
.I image
.B --recover --journal
.I directory
.SH DESCRIPTION
This experimental command grows or shrinks a regular exFAT volume image.
It does not change the container length or a partition table.
Direct block devices are disabled.
Prevent all other access. The file lock is advisory.
Visible Linux loop attachments are checked. Other namespaces and races can
limit this check.
.SH SIZE
Use an unsigned integer with B, KiB, MiB, GiB, or TiB.
The command rounds down to a whole filesystem sector.
It retains the cluster size. An equal rounded size is a checked no-op.
The filesystem must be at least 1 MiB. Metadata and retained allocations
can require a larger minimum. Use dry-run to check the target.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Run full read-only preflight. Print JSON geometry, relocation bounds, and
journal space. A shrink move count is exact. A growth move count is the
displaced prefix size and can include free clusters.
.TP
.B --info
Validate the current geometry and print its plan without writes.
.TP
.B --journal directory
Use a new directory for the external undo journal. Its parent must exist.
Reserve free space for the complete backing file plus 1 MiB.
The directory has mode 0700. Journal files have mode 0600 and contain file data.
The target must support user xattrs. Do not copy or delete an active journal.
.TP
.B --recover
Validate the journal and target identity. Restore the original image unless
a valid commit record selects the complete new image. Recovery can repeat
after interruption. A missing or corrupt journal cannot authorize writes.
Do not mount an image with an active transaction token.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: complete operation, valid plan, or completed recovery.
1: rejected input or failure without an active journal.
2: invalid command syntax.
3: active transaction; recovery is required.
4: committed image; cleanup did not complete.
130: handled cancellation. See the error message for the recovery state.
.SH LIMITS
Support is limited to Linux regular volume images at byte zero, exFAT revision
1.00, one FAT, and unchanged cluster size. TexFAT and unknown allocated entries
are rejected. A full old bitmap must fit during shrink. Growth needs space
for a new bitmap. Physical power-loss durability and direct devices are not
qualified. See docs/resize/README.md for support and test status.
.SH RECOVERY
Keep the backing file at its original length. Use the same file inode and
journal directory with --recover. If validation fails, stop and retain both.
A journal without a matching image token is stale. It must not be replayed.
After a cleanup failure with no image token, verify the image with fsck.exfat -n
and the independent reader before you remove the stale journal manually.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fsck.exfat (8),
.BR mkfs.exfat (8)
